# Every checkout gets the line ending git stored, never the one the host
# prefers. Text here is read by tools that match on "\n" (the RN shared
# contract check reads types.ts and asserts on multi-line literals) and by
# tools that must hash identical bytes on every host, and a Windows runner's
# core.autocrlf=true otherwise rewrites every file it checks out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep Windows project sources byte-stable across macOS, Linux, and Windows.
rn/NuGet.config text eol=lf

# The RN Windows generator owns this output, including its emitted spacing.
rn/apps/windows/windows/YoungRouter/codegen/** whitespace=-trailing-space
